# Security

## Auth

- Passwords: bcrypt/argon2. Cookie: HttpOnly, Secure (prod), SameSite=Lax.
- After password change invalidate the session. `is_active=false` blocks API and panel.
- Uniform login error message. No public registration.

## Authorization

- Mutating endpoints: role + `owner_id`. Admin only where intended.
- Public GET: only `PUBLISHED`/active. Drafts: author/admin.

## CSRF

- POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE with session → CSRF token. Exception only for login.

## SQL & validation

- ORM or parameterized queries only. Pydantic validation at the API boundary.
- URL: only `http:`/`https:`, reject `javascript:`, `data:`.
- Open redirect: relative paths from `/` only.

## XSS

- Autoescape in templates, `| safe` only from a trusted source.
- Client: `textContent` or `escapeHtml()`, not `innerHTML` from API.
- CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options.

## Upload

- Extension whitelist + magic bytes. Images: re-encode (PIL→JPEG).
- On-disk name: hash/UUID. Forbid `..` and leaving the upload dir. Size limits.

## Other

- Rate limiting: login (10-20/min), public writes, search.
- Secrets only from env/secret manager. Not in logs. TrustedHost in prod.
- SSRF: URL only from configuration. No pickle/eval/exec on user data.

## Tests

Check: anon/user/admin/inactive access, CSRF→403, path traversal, SQL/XSS injection, rate limit, open redirect.
